 "title": "Undo Paint",
 "body": "<p><strong>Goal:</strong> finish a <code>Stack</code> class and use it to give a drawing program an <strong>undo</strong> button. Every stroke you draw is pushed onto the stack. Pressing <code>u</code> pops the last stroke off and redraws the rest.</p>\n<ol type=\"1\">\n<li>Open <code>starter.py</code> in Thonny.</li>\n<li>Finish the four <code>TODO</code>s in <code>Stack</code> (<code>push</code>, <code>pop</code>, <code>peek</code>, <code>size</code>). The <code>Painter</code> class is done: read <code>move</code> and <code>undo</code> to see how it uses the stack.</li>\n<li>Press <strong>Run</strong>. Click on the turtle window first, then:\n<ul>\n<li>arrow keys draw,</li>\n<li><code>c</code> changes color (the color name is written at the top),</li>\n<li><code>u</code> undoes the last stroke. Press it several times!</li>\n</ul></li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Extra:</strong> add a REDO: when you undo, push the stroke onto a second stack called <code>redo_stack</code>. Pressing <code>r</code> pops from it and draws it again.</p>\n",
 "hints": [
